list-item.p:
a set of potential haploids, denoted 
      \mathrm{Haps}
      Haps,

a set of chromosomal loci, denoted 
      \mathrm{Loci}
      Loci, and

sec.p:
The set of all such haploid lineages is denoted 
    \mathrm{Haplins}
    Haplins.

A recombinant haploid tree process is a family of haploid tree valued random variables,
    index by time (with subscript) and locus (with superscript),

    \{ \mathrm{Tree}^\ell_t : t \in \Re, \ell \in \mathrm{Loci}\}
    {Treetℓ:t∈ℜ,ℓ∈Loci}
    such that

list-item.p:
for every 
        \ell \in \mathrm{Loci}
        ℓ∈Loci, 
        \{ \mathrm{Tree}^\ell_t : t \in \Re \}
        {Treetℓ:t∈ℜ} has a total increasing ordering
        under set inclusion order.

sec.p:
We start by defining the genetic legacy of an ancestral haploid

    h \in \mathrm{Haps}
    h∈Haps for a sample population 
    S \subseteq \mathrm{Haps}
    S⊆Haps to be

    \mathrm{Legacy}(h, S) := \{ (\ell, d) \in \mathrm{Loci}\times S : h \in \mathrm{Lin}(\ell, d) \}
    \text{ .}
    Legacy(h,S):={(ℓ,d)∈Loci×S:h∈Lin(ℓ,d)} .

A convenient choice for an embedded gARG6 is
    to set the gARG nodes (vertices) to be the equivalence classes:

    \mathrm{Nodes}(S) := \{ {[h]}_S : h \in \mathrm{Haps}\}
    \text{ .}
    Nodes(S):={[h]S:h∈Haps} .
